   737	    _spool_uuid minted on creation so body[i].spool_uuid sentinel matches.
   738	
   739	    iter2-P1-4: existing nonempty spool with empty header cache (PID reuse,
   740	    module reload, pytest reset) → parse existing header + reuse uuid;
   741	    minting a new one would produce header_body_uuid_mismatch quarantine.
   742	    iter4-P1-1: ordinal recovery via body-line parse (max(ordinal)+1), NOT
   743	    `\n` count — robust against unterminated final line from crashed writer.
   744	    iter4-P1-2: malformed-header → quarantine active spool via direct
   745	    rename (NOT drain_now() — Phase 2 self-deadlocks on our flock) +
   746	    fresh-mint retry (bounded depth=1).
